ƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxHhttps://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/19/could-ai-be-consciousƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Z2PESs_E0Wkgw6fSHVbZxKk_dVhMhz1pxBG4k2mSg7oƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9https://newscable-source-broker.invalid/activitypub/actorƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;niruSXWeQewM_6CqSZAPl8Ihxe1UP7FY3wmYFKBnst4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;1qX5OJrjm5Df0COnhZsoLb_zI3XGfDlsxisne-GOX4gƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxHhttps://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/19/could-ai-be-consciousƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;IZdjubH6H5JGa1JP4VqzBQidat1ImZ61hSQTS33OvjAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky»<p>Experts believe itâ€™s at least possible. We urgently need a plan to navigate the ethical implications</p><p>In January, the AI company Anthropic published a <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/constitution">new constitution</a> for Claude, its most advanced large language model (LLM), which contained the comment: â€œWe are caught in a difficult position where we neither want&nbsp;to&nbsp;overstate the likelihood of Claudeâ€™s moral patienthood nor dismiss it out of hand.â€ A month later, Anthropicâ€™s CEO Dario Amodei went on a podcast and said his company couldnâ€™t rule out the possibility that Claude was conscious. Philosopher David Chalmers, who coined the phrase â€œthe hard problem of consciousnessâ€, has said there is a significant chance of conscious LLMs within a decade. And what about Claude itself? When asked during testing to estimate the probability that it&nbsp;is a <em>moral patient</em>, meaning that its wellbeing matters&nbsp;in its own right, it gave numbers ranging from 5% to 40% and stressed how uncertain it was.</p><p>Modern AI systems are extraordinarily complex, and they are advancing fast. In terms of structural complexity and computational scale, by some measures a few are already in the range of a mouse brain, and at recent growth rates, they could reach the range of a human brain within five to 10 years.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/19/could-ai-be-conscious">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CzRoEXgqLrH56GBorgM87iCNt5PXo_RfHy9rI3y87SYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;P9vKmSD6SkMsmouZD1zLH_kyT_vmw5RmTJioMD2-sigƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CDq-WAetqlsPey_pAQb5LeB-FmOQJKFCyonKPW4jWkcƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;M-SNUasYqHKqAeg8-yHKITxrHHxCtOy8Y7heR-wQ5nwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;vseAJWt-tw0-GmJ0p_mzmcTpF43CgfAAsvXysAkVWTMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;X-J1sf7QfDVJS6Rpu6thVZ8j7ZxqCCg25CvciOpbmDUƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WYl319_23c1KMLvECFUPRDcc_5D0H1Ll9So9WFY_rT0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;jjB9grZF-Q5Ql6Fc_BL3oD4vnIpE4FQK1oaM-_shRMUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqSyndicationSourceƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WDZHZJr52D2